  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1039 PM MDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nRain and storms associated with the remnants of Polo has mostly \nexited the area but some lingering shower activity tonight is mostly \nassociated with a large upper low. The center of the upper low will \ntrek eastward through the day Wednesday but will only bring light \nshowery activity to the area as much of the moisture will be pushed \nout which will also kill instability. In addition, winds will become \nslightly breezier than what we've been seeing with west winds of 15-\n20 mph. Heading into Thursday, the upper low will be lifting out of \nthe southwest CONUS and into the Plains but models are consistently \ntrying to suggest some lingering energy behind the trough that may \nor may not pinch off into it's own low. Not much to say regarding \nthe weather right now heading into Friday and Saturday other than \nFriday will be slightly breezy, calm Saturday with chances for low \nend rain chances for the area mountains, more particularly for the \nSacramento Mtns. More breezy afternoons ahead for Sunday and Monday.",
